My boxes are standing in the hallway.
They are standing by the door to my new flat.
There are many boxes.
My friend Nina comes.
"Good morning, Maya!" she says.
"Good morning, Nina," I say.
Nina looks at the boxes.
"I'll help you," she says and smiles.
That is a big help.
The boxes are not heavy.
There are books and clothes in the boxes.
We take a box.
Then we take one more box.
Together we carry the boxes inside.
